course: dictionary
lesson: 10430
title: Trophy and the words around it
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A trophy is a prize, such as a cup, a shield or a statue, given to the winner of a competition. When you meet the word, read the words around it. «They lifted the trophy after the final» tells you the trophy is something won and held up high.
explain: A trophy can also be something kept to remember a success, such as a hunting trophy. The clues are different here: the thing is kept as a sign of what someone did. Ask yourself what would fit in the sentence, then try your meaning in place of the word.
explain: Small words like «it» point back to another word. In «The trophy didn't fit in the suitcase because it was too big», it means the trophy. Change one word to «too small» and it now means the suitcase. Read the whole sentence to find out which one it means.
fact: A trophy is a prize such as a cup, a shield or a statue, given to a winner.
fact: Trophies are often kept in a «trophy cabinet», so people can remember a success.
fact: «Win a trophy» and «lift the trophy» are common phrases. To lift means to raise something up.
fact: A «hunting trophy» is something kept to remember a success in hunting.
fact: Games, phones and apps keep records such as trophies, dates and history, and these can settle arguments.
exercise: «They lifted the trophy high after the final.» What is a trophy here? | A kind of sandwich eaten at lunch | A quiet place to read | A school bag with wheels | *A prize, such as a cup, given to a winner
exercise: «The trophy didn't fit in the suitcase because it was too big.» What does it mean? | *The trophy | The suitcase | The cabinet | The winner
exercise: Where are trophies often kept so people can remember a success? | Under the bed in a shoebox | *In a trophy cabinet | In the rain outside | In the bin after sports day
test: «The hunter kept the antlers as a trophy.» What does trophy mean here? | *Something kept to remember a success | A map of the hills | A kind of weather | A rubbish bin
test: What can settle an argument about who scored the most goals? | Guessing and shouting | A loud voice | Changing the rules halfway through | *Records such as trophies, dates and history
exam: What is a trophy, as in «win a trophy»? | A type of sandwich | A kind of school bag | *A prize, such as a cup or shield, given to a winner | A quiet walk in the park
